 "description": "You are given a partly filled 9 x 9 Sudoku `board`. Each cell holds a digit `\"1\"` to `\"9\"` or `\".\"` for empty. Return `True` if the filled cells follow the rules:\n\n- no digit repeats in any row,\n- no digit repeats in any column, and\n- no digit repeats in any of the nine 3 x 3 boxes.\n\nYou only need to check the filled cells. The board does not need to be solvable.",
 "function": "isValidSudoku",
 "params": [
  "board"
 ],
 "starter": "class Solution:\n    def isValidSudoku(self, board: List[List[str]]) -> bool:\n        pass\n",
 "hints": [
  "Check rows, columns and boxes separately, using a set to spot repeats.",
  "The 3 x 3 box for cell `(r, c)` can be identified by `(r // 3, c // 3)`.",
  "In a single pass, keep a set per row, per column and per box. If a digit is already in any of the three sets for its cell, return `False`."
